# TaxOps hard invariants — never break these

## Email architecture (holding-area model — since `pre-email-simplification` tag)

- Pipeline: IMAP → `mail_watcher._save_to_inbox()` → `email_inbox` (unassigned) →
  staff manually assigns via `/email-inbox` UI → `/api/email-inbox/<id>/assign` →
  `return_documents` (+ extraction enqueued).
- There is no automated sender classifier, fuzzy client matching, or confirmation
  queue in this architecture. `known_sender_rules`, `_save_attachments`,
  `_update_domain_cache`, and `/api/email-review/*` no longer exist — do not
  reintroduce references to them. Historical implementation is preserved at git
  tag `pre-email-simplification` if that system is ever revived.
- Archived (dead, do not read/write): `archive_email_classifications`,
  `archive_domain_classifications` — see the migration that renamed them.

## Email read/unread status

- **`_mark_read` is a tombstone — never call it.**
- All IMAP fetches use `BODY.PEEK[]`, never `RFC822` (which auto-sets `\Seen` on Gmail).
- `email_processing_log` is the restart-safe dedup layer — checked every poll, unconditionally.
- No `-FLAGS \Seen` STORE call exists anywhere and none may be added.

## Email match confirmation (rewritten — staff assignment IS the confirmation)

- Email-assign path (`/api/email-inbox/<id>/assign` in `app.py`): must explicitly set
  `match_confirmed=1, match_score=NULL, match_method='email_manual'`. Never omit these
  columns and rely on the schema default — that silent-drift bug is what this rule exists
  to prevent.
- Walk-in uploads via `routes/documents.py` must have `match_confirmed=1, match_method='manual'`.
- `match_confirmed=0` is reserved for a future path where software proposes a match a human
  has not yet ratified. No such path currently exists — do not set it to 0 anywhere today.

## Suppression rules (sender allow/block)

- Suppression stays LLM-free and does **at most one** rules `SELECT` per poll cycle (cache
  in memory, refresh once per cycle) — never a per-message DB read.
- Precedence: explicit staff **allow** > explicit staff **block** > Drive-share suppression >
  hardcoded `KNOWN_PROMOTIONAL_DOMAINS`/`MASS_MAILING_PREFIXES` > default pass-through.
- Personal email domains (gmail.com, yahoo.com, icloud.com, etc.) can only be blocked at the
  full-address level, never at the domain level.

## Vision extraction

- `EXTRACTOR_VISION_ENABLED` defaults to `false`.
- When false, `.jpg/.jpeg/.png` files return `(None, "image_skipped")` from `_extract_fields`
  and the queue row gets `status='skipped'` — never `'failed'`, never retried.

## Privacy

- `file_path`, `ssn_last4`, and identification numbers are never returned in any API response.
- Email body is never stored in any DB column.
- `BODY.PEEK[]` ensures email body content never touches server flags.
- `scrub_ssn_from_dict()` is applied to all user-supplied filenames before they touch disk or DB.
- `IMAP_PASS` is never logged, printed, or rendered in any UI (including admin health panels).

## DB migrations

- New columns go in `_migrate_existing_tables()` in `db.py`, never in `init_db()` only.
- Always use `ALTER TABLE … ADD COLUMN` with a safe default so existing rows stay valid.
- Every schema change is a numbered migration, tested against a DB copy first
  (`PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE);` then copy `.db`/`-wal`/`-shm`, run, `PRAGMA integrity_check;`).

## Watcher thread safety

- Single-start guard (`_watcher_started`) must be preserved — the Flask dev-server reloader
  must never spawn a second poll thread.
